    <string name="section_about">About</string>
    <string name="action_about">About &amp; privacy</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s (%2$d)</string>
    <string name="about_purpose">API Manager is a private vault for the API endpoints and secret keys you use for your own projects. Add a provider, paste its base URL and key, and the key is encrypted on your device before it is stored.</string>
    <string name="about_security">Security: AES-256-GCM encryption with a key held in the Android Keystore. Optional PIN / fingerprint lock. Backups contain encrypted keys only and never leave your device unless you export them. Device-to-device transfers use a one-time code to re-encrypt keys for the receiving device. Deleted entries stay in Trash for 14 days and are then removed automatically.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy">Privacy: we collect nothing. There are no accounts, no analytics, no ads and no Google Play services. The internet permission is used only for the optional local-network transfer between two of your devices. Google AI Mode or Brave AI searches open in your own browser; we do not host a search backend or an API catalogue.</string>
